#!/bin/bash
# info: update system queue
# options: QUEUE
# labels: internal
# caller: cron
#
# example: h-update-sys-queue restart
#
# Runs the queued jobs of one pipe, so ten domain changes restart a service once.

queue=$1

# shellcheck source=/etc/hestia/hestia.env
source /etc/hestia/hestia.env
# shellcheck source=/usr/local/hestia/include/main.sh
source $HESTIA/include/main.sh
source_conf "$HESTIA/conf/hestia.conf"

check_args '1' "$#" 'QUEUE'

b_task=$(ps auxf | grep -v "grep" | grep "$BIN/h-update-sys-queue backup")
b_task=$(echo "$b_task" | grep -v sudo | wc -l)
if [ "$b_task" -gt 2 ]; then
	exit
fi

case $queue in
	restart) bash $CONF_DIR/queue/$queue.pipe > /dev/null 2>&1 ;;
	webstats) bash $CONF_DIR/queue/$queue.pipe > /dev/null 2>&1 ;;
	backup) bash $CONF_DIR/queue/$queue.pipe > /dev/null 2>&1 ;;
	disk) bash $CONF_DIR/queue/$queue.pipe > /dev/null 2>&1 ;;
	daily) bash $CONF_DIR/queue/$queue.pipe > /dev/null 2>&1 ;;
	traffic) bash $CONF_DIR/queue/$queue.pipe > /dev/null 2>&1 ;;
	*) check_args '1' '0' 'QUEUE' ;;
esac

exit
